{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we start by analyzing the given geometric configuration. We have two isosceles triangles \\( \\triangle ABC \\) and \\( \\triangle ABD \\) with \\( AB = AC = BD \\), and \\( \\overline{BD} \\perp \\overline{AC} \\). The intersection point of \\( \\overline{BD} \\) and \\( \\overline{AC} \\) is \\( E \\).\n\nFirst, let's determine the angles in \\( \\triangle ABD \\). Since \\( BD \\perp AC \\), \\( \\angle BEC = 90^\\circ \\). Because \\( \\triangle ABD \\) is isosceles with \\( AB = BD \\), the base angles \\( \\angle BAD \\) and \\( \\angle ABD \\) are equal. Let \\( \\angle BAD = \\angle ABD = x \\). Then, the vertex angle \\( \\angle ADB \\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\angle ADB = 180^\\circ - 2x\n\\]\n\nNext, we consider \\( \\triangle ABC \\). Since \\( \\triangle ABC \\) is isosceles with \\( AB = AC \\), the base angles \\( \\angle ABC \\) and \\( \\angle ACB \\) are equal. Let \\( \\angle ABC = \\angle ACB = y \\). Then, the vertex angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\angle BAC = 180^\\circ - 2y\n\\]\n\nSince \\( E \\) is the intersection of \\( BD \\) and \\( AC \\), we can use the fact that \\( \\angle AEB = 90^\\circ \\) (as \\( BD \\perp AC \\)). This implies that \\( \\angle AED = 90^\\circ \\).\n\n","prefix_end":1148,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1191,553,41018,279,2661,52484,6546,13,1205,614,1378,374,436,346,642,42446,17767,1124,55114,19360,1124,8,323,17767,1124,55114,362,9548,1124,8,448,17767,14137,284,10584,284,39310,1124,701,323,17767,1124,1975,1056,90,9548,92,1124,712,79,1124,1975,1056,90,1706,92,1124,568,576,19246,1459,315,17767,1124,1975,1056,90,9548,92,1124,8,323,17767,1124,1975,1056,90,1706,92,1124,8,374,17767,468,1124,3593,5338,11,1077,594,8253,279,25941,304,17767,1124,55114,362,9548,1124,568,8704,17767,39310,1124,712,79,10584,1124